    {
      "requirement_id": "008-settings-cli:AC-001",
      "disposition": "covered",
      "rationale": "The executable boundary, supported platforms, Windows console attachment, preserved flags and prohibited GUI/model side effects are explicit and observable; the read budget names hardware and release mode. This defines a feasible CLI branch before ordinary application startup, with platform regression proof still to be planned.",
      "source_citations": [
        {
          "section_id": ".specs/features/008-settings-cli/spec.md:L206-L210",
          "excerpt": "A `handy settings` invocation never shows a window, a tray icon or loads a model, never triggers the single-instance \"show window\" behavior, and completes reads within 2 seconds on an Apple M1 Mac in a release build."
        }
      ],
      "plan_citations": [],
      "searched_plan_sections": []
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "008-settings-cli:AC-002",
      "disposition": "covered",
      "rationale": "Read/discovery/scalar write behavior is explicit, including descriptor parsing, unknown keys, secret presence-only output, refusal of list/secret/read-only writes, equivalent JSON flag placement and a read-only missing-store path. Selecting the actual descriptor catalog is a legitimate technical plan decision.",
      "source_citations": [
        {
          "section_id": ".specs/features/008-settings-cli/spec.md:L211-L215",
          "excerpt": "`set` parses VALUE with the key's descriptor type (boolean `true`/`false`, integer, enumeration value, string). Generic `set` on a list key returns `validation_failed` naming the domain command to use; on a secret or read-only key it returns `validation_failed` stating that the key is changed in the settings UI."
        }
      ],
      "plan_citations": [],
      "searched_plan_sections": []
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "008-settings-cli:AC-003",
      "disposition": "covered",
      "rationale": "One backend validator is authoritative for both surfaces, with stable English errors, translated presentation and rejection replacing historical fallback. Rejected writes preserve settings. Tests can use the same value matrix through UI commands and CLI rather than duplicate validators.",
      "source_citations": [
        {
          "section_id": ".specs/features/008-settings-cli/spec.md:L216-L220",
          "excerpt": "Every write goes through the same backend validation functions as the corresponding UI command, so a value the UI rejects is rejected by the CLI with the same error code and English message, and vice versa; the UI may show that message translated."
        }
      ],
      "plan_citations": [],
      "searched_plan_sections": []
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "008-settings-cli:AC-004",
      "disposition": "covered",
      "rationale": "The revision contract distinguishes actual changes from no-ops and reads, covers every writer, defines conflict detail location and requires locked reread before patching. The concurrency scenario and SC-002 provide a falsifiable lost-update oracle. Cross-process locking and atomic store replacement remain implementation choices.",
      "source_citations": [
        {
          "section_id": ".specs/features/008-settings-cli/spec.md:L221-L225",
          "excerpt": "All writers (UI commands, a running instance and a headless CLI process) are serialized by one cross-process settings lock, and each writer re-reads the stored settings under that lock before applying its change, so a write without expected revision applies to the latest settings and never discards fields changed by another writer."
        }
      ],
      "plan_citations": [],
      "searched_plan_sections": []
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "008-settings-cli:AC-005",
      "disposition": "covered",
      "rationale": "Identity is scoped to the same user and settings store; live routing, timeout with unknown outcome, older-version refusal and headless fallback are all explicit. No-answer never authorizes another writer. User-only permissions and no network listener constrain the transport; its concrete per-platform mechanism belongs in the plan.",
      "source_citations": [
        {
          "section_id": ".specs/features/008-settings-cli/spec.md:L226-L230",
          "excerpt": "If no answer arrives in time, the CLI returns `unavailable` with `error.details.outcome` set to `unknown`, and agents must read again before retrying. If a running Handy without this channel (an older version) is detected, the CLI returns `unavailable` and never writes the store itself."
        }
      ],
      "plan_citations": [],
      "searched_plan_sections": []
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "008-settings-cli:AC-006",
      "disposition": "covered",
      "rationale": "The foundation owns the shared parsing/input/dry-run/commit/help framework and existing output settings. New smart paste and automatic Enter belong to later owner features, and help must match the actual build. Clarifications resolve the replacement/destination examples as downstream scenarios with a test-only fixture for 008.",
